  "source_excerpts": {
    "title": "Disjoint target routing among overlapping factor-base charts",
    "mechanism": "Object: a disjoint target partition with a costed solver chart attached to each cell. Operation set Sigma: evaluate the public routing predicate, dispatch the target to its assigned chart, and pull back a decomposition certificate. Trichotomy: coordinate-dependent; this is a solver/representation object, not a lossy quotient under the full group translation action. Discarded information: within a routing cell the predicate discards target details; the full target remains the solver input, so no false deterministic quotient action is claimed. Start with overlapping high-degree/implicit digit factor bases whose union size is frozen. Search a bounded family of coordinate predicates that predicts which chart has cheaper decomposition work. Make routing disjoint by an explicit priority rule, charge unsuccessful routing and descent, and evaluate against the best fixed chart with the same total base storage. Conservation of mean tuples remains exact; only conditional cost can change.",
    "minimal_test": {
      "design": "m=3, interval/digit charts on three ordinary prime-field curves, N about 2^12,2^16,2^20; at most eight routing predicates selected on a separate fully charged calibration set, then frozen.",
      "execution_status": "design_only_not_approved",
      "controls": [
        {
          "kind": "baseline",
          "design": "One chart and constant router give the original fixed-chart solver exactly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "matched_null",
          "design": "Random relabeling of chart/target associations, matched union size and overlap pattern."
        },
        {
          "kind": "known_false",
          "design": "A routing oracle that reads a planted decomposition or hidden scalar is inadmissible; two identical charts must give zero gain before routing overhead."
        },
        {
          "kind": "identity",
          "design": "Use the stated baseline slice with identical inputs, ordering and certificate policy; output identities must match exactly."
        },
        {
          "kind": "generic_group",
          "design": "For any claimed group information gain, repeat the statistic on relabelled Z/NZ with the same incidence and acquisition budget. Algebra-only comparisons explicitly do not claim a generic-group escape."
        }
      ],
      "required_metrics": [
        "routing cost, conditional solve cost, target coverage, informative rank by chart",
        "all setup, acquisition, unsuccessful-attempt, transport, certificate and verification costs",
        "peak resident memory and total stored bytes",
        "SAT and UNSAT costs separately, or successful and failed incidence attempts separately",
        "loss L=log2(number of represented preimages) and branching b=max verified successors at each retained synopsis; witness storage separately"
      ],
      "budget": {
        "proposed_only": true,
        "maximum_runs": 0,
        "note": "This handoff approves zero runs. A successor needs a new frozen per-cell budget; planning allowance 3 implementation-days and up to 4 CPU-hours/32 GiB for first complete toy cell, scaled only by Coordinator approval. Exhaustive synthetic calibrators may warrant smaller documented bounds."
      },
      "stopping_rules": [
        "Stop on first soundness/completeness control failure and classify the instrument invalid.",
        "At a frozen resource cap report failed_infrastructure without a mathematical verdict.",
        "If valid completed cells miss the quantitative threshold, reject only this mechanism/parameter claim and retain the measured obstruction."
      ],
      "required_artifacts": [
        "frozen source formula/curve/base and seeds",
        "all candidate descriptions and failed attempts",
        "exact control and solution certificates",
        "stage-cost and memory records",
        "independent checker source binding",
        "unpooled raw metrics"
      ]
    },
    "falsification_conditions": [
      "Any valid completed cell exhibits the known-false failure: A routing oracle that reads a planted decomposition or hidden scalar is inadmissible; two identical charts must give zero gain before routing overhead.",
      "The completed controlled ladder fails the proposed effect: C_route+E[C_selected] <=0.8 min_j E[C_j] after common setup, including failed targets",
      "The charged saving disappears after including construction, canonicalization, failed attempts, memory or recovery.",
      "A purported synopsis merges the collision pair without retaining its distinction: Equal branch-stratum counts with different open-locus conditional costs require the retained open residual, not a monodromy-only prediction."
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "Public generated mathematical instances only, with frozen field, subgroup, curve, factor-base definition, presentation, solver and sample law.",
      "F2 factor-base decomposition is a component, not the proposed new object; the added object is a disjoint target partition with a costed solver chart attached to each cell. F1 generic search is a comparator; any F7 caching/preprocessing is fully charged.",
      "All identity, soundness and completeness certificates must be independently checked before measuring cost.",
      "Prime-field digit/implicit membership is a high-degree or implicit-description escape class of KN-OPEN-020, not a bounded-degree plane-locus exemption. Binary arms use actual Weil descent and never transfer Boolean identities to F_p."
    ],
    "proof_search_map": {
      "bottleneck": "The exact load-bearing step is producing and using a disjoint target partition with a costed solver chart attached to each cell cheaply enough for: C_route+E[C_selected] <=0.8 min_j E[C_j] after common setup, including failed targets",
      "baseline_embedding": {
        "parameter_slice": "One chart and constant router give the original fixed-chart solver exactly.",
        "reproduction_check": "First prove this equality symbolically; in a successor compare every output/certificate at the smallest exhaustive fixture. No reproduction was executed in this task."
      },
