          "predicted_gain": "C_route+E[C_selected] <=0.8 min_j E[C_j] after common setup, including failed targets"
        }
      ],
      "quantifier_order": "For every admitted public instance in the frozen parameter family, construct certificates with soundness and completeness; for the preregistered distribution and selected fixed design, H1 predicts C_route+E[C_selected] <=0.8 min_j E[C_j] after common setup, including failed targets. Selection may depend on public parameters and charged calibration, never on hidden scalar labels or evaluation outcomes.",
      "method_ceiling": {
        "strongest_certifiable_claim": "A publicly computable disjoint routing rule may improve charged target-solving cost by >=20% at the same union-base size and target distribution, without changing the conserved total tuple count. A successful finite test is scoped evidence only; a uniform asymptotic theorem requires a separate bound on every growth parameter.",
        "nearby_object_control": "A routing oracle that reads a planted decomposition or hidden scalar is inadmissible; two identical charts must give zero gain before routing overhead."
